oc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> </patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>None</text><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1090786A1</text><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIGUCHI TOSHIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI HEAVY IND LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIJIMA HIDEYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIGUCHI, TOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI HEAVY INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIJIMA, HIDEYA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIGUCHI TOSHIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIJIMA HIDEYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIGUCHI, TOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIJIMA, HIDEYA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A heat pump type air conditioner for vehicle capable of increasing a comfortableness in a cabin by minimizing a defrosting operation during a heating operation, comprising an indoor heat exchanger (10) performing a heat exchange between refrigerant and cabin air, outdoor heat exchangers (41, 42) performing a heat exchange between refrigerant and outside air, and a compressor unit (20) having a compressor (21), a restriction resistance (22), and a four-way valve (23), all connected to each other through a refrigerant flow path (60) to perform the cooling and heating operations by switching the flow direction of the refrigerant, characterized in that the plurality of outdoor heat exchangers (41, 42) are disposed on both sides of a radiator (30) in parallel with each other.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un conditionneur d'air de type pompe à chaleur pour véhicule conçu pour accroître le confort dans une cabine en réduisant une opération de dégivrage pendant le chauffage, qui comprend un échangeur thermique intérieur (10) assurant un échange thermique entre un réfrigérant et l'air de la cabine, des échangeurs thermiques extérieurs (41, 42) assurant un échange thermique entre un réfrigérant et l'air extérieur, et une unité de compression (20) pourvue d'un compresseur (21), d'une résistance de restriction (22) et d'un robinet à quatre voies (23), tous reliés les uns autres par une voie d'écoulement (60) du réfrigérant pour assurer les opérations de refroidissement et de chauffage par commutation de la direction de l'écoulement du réfrigérant, la pluralité des échangeurs thermiques extérieurs (41, 42) étant placés sur les deux côtés d'un radiateur (30) disposés parallèlement les uns aux autres.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this